## Why this is decisive for route C2, on its own

Route C2 has **no EE measurement of any kind**, and declaration v1.9 §5 already states its
**set-level oracle marginal is zero by construction** — its certificate is forecast validity,
not a selection marginal. So the only question that can settle C2 today is: **can a head
predict the declared C2 target from decision-time information?** If it cannot, route C2 is
finished as declared, with no panel, no corpus and no EE run required.

Note also that the shipped corpus's "C2" is a surrogate, and `ORACLE-FACTORIAL`'s "C2" is an
ACM-rung control term. **Neither is the declared target.** The declared target is
`c2_persistence_forecast` (`physics_v025/targets.py:251-310`): OPS-3-style absorbing
persistence over the three sealed offsets, with one `-kappa` per lost offset.

