# C2REAL protocol reconstruction

Completion criterion: this note identifies the C1REAL sampling/training/metric/bootstrap
protocol and every source-backed change required to apply it to declared C2, without
treating either shipped-C2 or ORACLE-FACTORIAL C2 as the declared target.

## What must be copied from C1REAL

- **Sample and exact path.** C1REAL generated 39 exact-path anchors (19 in
  `V025_PROBE/world/1`, 20 in `V025_PROBE/world/2`) but modeled a coherent 37-anchor
  prefix: world 1 steps 0--17 and world 2 steps 0--18, 36,360 rows and 3,700
  `(anchor,user)` groups. Two shutdown-race anchors were verification/timing only. Its
  exact-path timing was mean 474.75 s/anchor, median 401.64 s, IQR 380.37--434.95 s,
  range 343.27--1,721.77 s. The requested 60 were not reached, and LOWO has only two
  world clusters. [C1REAL report, lines 44--65](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/C1-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-2026-09-10.md)
- **Setting and carrier.** Import `scripts.run_v025_pilot_c3.py`, set
  `PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK = False` on that imported module object, then call
  `_build_anchor_rows`; use setting `a-r0`, carrier `nearest-eligible`, shipped shortlist
  support, 100 users, calibrated pilot values, and boundary indices `(0,)`. C1REAL left
  the source literal `True` on disk. [C1REAL report, lines 35--42](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/C1-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-2026-09-10.md)
  The source confirms that `False` bypasses the primitive branch and enters the dormant
  evaluator/three-offset-forecast path at line 544; that path uses `boundary_indices=(0,)`
  and `_batched_stage2_forecasts`. [`scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:525-580`](../../scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py)
  For C2REAL, additionally hash the pilot source bytes immediately before import/work and
  after completion and assert equality, because the present request explicitly requires a
  byte-identity assertion (C1REAL only reported that it did not edit the file).
- **Pair construction and cap.** Within every training fold, pair every non-reference row
  with the unique reference/BASE row of its `(anchor,user)` group and train on target
  differences. If the fold has more than 4,096 candidates, retain the deterministic
  `np.linspace(0, n-1, 4096, dtype=int64)` aggregate. [`learner.py:217-259`](../../src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py)
  and [`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1149-1163`](../../scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py). C1REAL's
  cross-validation implementation performs the cap after restricting to the training
  fold. [`C1 analyze.py:123-150`](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/.scratch/c1-declared/analyze.py)
- **Folds and seeds.** Make one outer fold per anchor for LOAO and one per world for LOWO.
  C1REAL used only the first sealed pilot learner seed for LOAO
  (`V025_LEARNER/seed/1`, integer `6407676579069309528`) and reported the arithmetic mean
  over all four pilot seeds for LOWO, preserving per-seed values/ranges in JSON.
  [C1REAL report, lines 89--101](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/C1-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-2026-09-10.md)
- **Metrics.** Pool all out-of-fold predictions before scoring. Level `R^2` is raw head
  score versus normalized target, includes exact-zero BASE rows, and has no test-time
  regauging. Ordering uses every within-`(anchor,user)` pair whose true difference exceeds
  `1e-12` in absolute value; correct signs get 1, predicted ties (`<=1e-15`) get 0.5.
  Top-1 uses stable `np.argmax` and counts a hit when the chosen row's truth is within
  `1e-12` of the group maximum. [`C1 analyze.py:153-186`](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/.scratch/c1-declared/analyze.py)
  and [C1REAL report, lines 103--110](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/C1-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-2026-09-10.md).
- **Bootstrap.** Use 2,000 anchor-cluster bootstrap replicates. C1REAL pre-aggregated each
  anchor's row sums/squares/RSS, ordering credit/comparable-pair count, and top-1
  hits/group count; each replicate samples the same number of anchors with replacement and
  reports percentile 2.5/97.5 intervals plus bootstrap SE. Its fixed bootstrap seed domain
  was `C1REAL/anchor-bootstrap/2026-09-10`; C2 should use an analogous C2REAL domain so the
  procedure is identical without recycling the random stream. [`C1 analyze.py:408-481`](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/.scratch/c1-declared/analyze.py)
  C1REAL applied this bootstrap only to the primary sealed LOAO prediction
  ([`C1 analyze.py:593-603`](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/.scratch/c1-declared/analyze.py));
  the present C2 request can reasonably be read more strictly as requiring all three
  intervals for both LOAO and LOWO. If LOWO is anchor-bootstrapped, label it as within-panel
  uncertainty only: two worlds do not support a population-of-worlds interval.

## True C2 deviations

1. **The target is declared persistence, not either object called C2 elsewhere.** The row
   builder calls `c2_persistence_forecast(candidate projections, base projections, ...)`
   and stores `forecast_surplus_bits - persistence_penalty_bits`; source-row extraction
   divides that bits value by the anchor's `kappa`.
   [`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:599-607,674-677`](../../scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py) and
   [`state.py:435-481`](../../src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py). Do not fit or contrast the
   shipped surrogate or ORACLE-FACTORIAL control term as though either were this label.
   Consequently, C1REAL's surrogate and `Phi`-only rows are omitted; the required references
   here are sealed head, same-objective linear fit, training-fold constant, and a flexible
   same-input model.
2. **Absorbing structure.** The helper requires exactly three ordered candidate and default
   projections. It accumulates physical surplus only while alive; a failed current offset
   increments `lost`, and every later offset is also a loss. It subtracts `kappa * lost`, so
   `normalized_total = core/kappa - lost`, with `lost in {0,1,2,3}`.
   [`targets.py:251-310`](../../src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py). Verify the stored label
   independently by reconstructing the same singleton forecast and calling the helper, as
   the production acceptance test does. [`test_c1c2_exact_label_acceptance.py:200-232`](../../tests/stagec_v025/test_c1c2_exact_label_acceptance.py)
   Also verify exact-zero BASE gauge. Unlike C1, report counts/fractions by `lost_offsets`,
   exact target-value masses (especially `0,-1,-2,-3`), unique-value count/quantiles, and
   tied versus non-tied within-group pair counts. This prevents a modal absorbing floor from
   masquerading as ordering skill.
3. **Inputs are the 22-slot `q2_state`.** The schema is ten current features followed by
   four fields (`valid`, `survival`, minimum decoding margin, mean ACM SE) at each of three
   offsets. [`state.py:48-66,82-86`](../../src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py). The extractor
   defines the exact raw order and normalization at [`state.py:414-456`](../../src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py).
   Seven Q1 fields reappear explicitly: Q1 7->Q2 2 (D2 time), 8->3 (visibility), 9->4
   (refresh), 3->5 (occupancy), 4->6 (beam-active), 5->7 (satellite-active), and 15->9
   (missing incumbent). Q1REAL found Q1 slots 6 and 15 constant and Q1 pairs 3/4 and 11/12
   exactly redundant [C1REAL report, lines 201--205](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/C1-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-2026-09-10.md),
   so constant Q1 slot 15 necessarily propagates to Q2 slot 9, and Q2 slots 5/6 inherit the
   occupancy/indicator redundancy. In this builder, both Q1 0 and Q2 0 are populated from
   `profile.min_decoding_margin_db`, and Q2 8 is derived from the same required-power value
   used in Q1 1; audit these as observed row-level equal/affine relations rather than silently
   assuming schema-level identity. [`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:630-665`](../../scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py).
   Before any fit, report every exact constant, exact duplicate/indicator/affine relation,
   numerical matrix rank, and effective dimension. Do not simply claim `22`.
4. **The sealed head changes materially.** Use `AdamMLPHead` with C2 literals: hidden
   `(100,50,50)`, tanh, learning rate `1e-3`, Adam betas `(0.9,0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`,
   zero weight decay, `gauge_beta=0.1`, loss weight 1, 2,000 exact epochs, one deterministic
   full-batch route update per source epoch, no early selection.
   [`learner.py:39-65`](../../src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py). The implementation is pairwise
   candidate-minus-reference squared error plus the reference-zero gauge, optimized by Adam.
   [`learner.py:658-791`](../../src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py). The acceptance test confirms
   C2 layer shapes `(22,100),(100,50),(50,50),(50,1)`.
   [`test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:444-451`](../../tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py)
5. **References/capacity.** The linear reference must solve the same pairwise objective and
   use `sqrt(0.1)` gauge rows, not C1's `sqrt(0.2)` and not ordinary scalar regression. The
   constant remains each training fold's mean target; its ordering is 0.5 by tie credit and
   its stable-argmax top-1 must be printed explicitly. When widening the sealed head, retain
   its three tanh hidden layers and change widths only (for example proportional variants
   around `(100,50,50)`), keeping optimizer, epochs, cap, gauge, and seeds fixed. For the
   C1-style high-capacity probe, changing 16 raw slots to 22 makes the random-feature design
   535 columns/parameters (`22 + 256 + 256 + 1`), with ridge selected inside each outer
   training fold from `{0.01,0.1,1,10,100,1000}` on training-only held-out anchors.
   [`C1 analyze.py:270-348`](../../../mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/.scratch/c1-declared/analyze.py).
   Call this the best **observed empirical** same-input fit, not a proof of the Bayes ceiling.
6. **No EE inference.** Declaration v1.9 says C2's set-level oracle effect may be zero by
   construction and that its physics certificate is forecast validity, while learned-stage
   Q2 shapes proposals. [Declaration v1.9, item 5](../../../mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.9-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md).
   This run therefore measures only held-out prediction of the declared target; losses and
   predictive metrics make no EE claim.

## Reporting shape to retain

Open with one bold sentence containing modeled/generated anchors, held-out ordering, level
`R^2`, sealed top-1 versus constant top-1, and informational-versus-architectural reading.
Then print `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`; define `[RUN]`, `[DERIVED]`, `[INFERRED]`; state the no-EE
scope; report exact-row budget/timing and power limitations; target verification and C2
distribution/ties; effective dimension **before fits**; exact fit/metric definitions; a
LOAO/LOWO table for sealed, linear, constant, widened heads, and high-capacity model;
capacity-versus-information interpretation; and reproducibility paths/digests/validator and
peak RSS. This mirrors the C1REAL report's structure while replacing its C1-only surrogate,
`Phi`, and 16-slot analyses with C2's absorbing-target and 22-slot analyses.
